  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "Some WebM videos encoded with VP9 display green visual corruption when played in VRChat on AMD graphics hardware.\n\nIn our testing, this issue has only occurred on AMD hardware. It has been reproduced on:\n\n- AMD A10 APUs\n\n- AMD Radeon RX 6800\n\n- AMD Radeon RX 6900\n\n- Some AMD Radeon RX 7000 series GPUs\n\nOther video formats we have tested do not exhibit this issue.\n\nSteps to reproduce:\n\n1. Launch VRChat through Steam without the --disable-hw-video-decoding launch option on an affected AMD system.\n\n2. Play an affected WebM video encoded with VP9.\n\n3. Observe green visual corruption during playback.\n\nExpected behavior:\n\nWebM videos encoded with VP9 should play correctly with the default settings.\n\nActual behavior:\n\nAffected videos display green visual corruption on the AMD hardware listed above.\n\nWorkaround:\n\nAdd the following option in Steam > VRChat > Properties > Launch Options:\n\n--disable-hw-video-decoding\n\nThen fully restart VRChat. After applying this option, the same videos play correctly.\n\nThese results suggest a possible issue with hardware-accelerated VP9 decoding on AMD graphics hardware, although the underlying cause has not been confirmed.",
